Here is why I love Levy's usual video format: 
Simple and clear to watch him communicating;
No silly or stupid editing with loud sound effects, just him talking and the moves;
No cuts, which makes the video as a whole more professional.
I'd like people to stick more often to this type of format, especially on educative videos like these.
(Post Note: There is a clear contrast with the thumbnails and the video format, which is hilarious.)
